== Vendor-model and mutation checks (scratch, not committed) ==
ORFS vendor OpenRAM .v (all three macros; $display stripped, posedge
`dout = 'bx` made non-blocking, see gen_openram_models.py) under
Verilator --no-timing --x-assign/--x-initial unique, on 035bb05:
  vec_tb: VEC TB PASS on +verilator+seed 1, 2, 3
  run_directed.sh on the cached core_tb: 36 PASS lines, 0 FAIL
  (Adding +verilator+rand+reset+2 trips the `ifndef SYNTHESIS
  estimate cross-check in muserisc_vec.sv:780 at time 0 on random
  pre-reset state; the plain behavioural vec_tb does the same, so it
  is not a macro issue. Noted for #20.)
  (Earlier, on 910c023: with the vendor's blocking posedge `dout = 'bx`
  the same-edge capture flop races it in zero-delay simulation and the
  vector TB fails, ~3,070 failures.)
Mutations of the wrappers (on 910c023; wrapper RTL unchanged since):
  VRF capture register removed: VEC TB FAIL on both families
    (fakeram45 3054, sky130 1585 failures)
  VRF sky130 read select inverted / fakeram45 byte mask from wbe[0] only:
    VEC TB FAIL (23062 / 9426 failures)
  L1 sky130 half select stuck at low half: 4/4 cache directed tests FAIL
  L1 capture register removed: full directed suite still PASSES (the
    caches consume array data the cycle after the read); the register is
    kept because muserisc_sram_sp documents the hold.
